            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "> As per the README, mini.completion is supposed to also handle mini.snippets snippets, but they are not visible in the completion menu.\n\nYes, 'mini.completion' does work with 'mini.snippets', as in it used by default when *inserting* snippet candidates from LSP server. To have snippets that are *loaded* via 'mini.snippets' be present as completion candidates in 'mini.completion', indeed execute `MiniSnippets.start_lsp_server()`. This is [documented](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/e38547768b2e12bdd48b16b8cfdca2e3b7543e22/doc/mini-snippets.txt#L32-L34).\n\nSo basically what @krovuxdev said :)\n\nClosing as working as expected.",
